{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7312052","formula":"C₂₆H₃₈N₂O₉","hill":"C26H38N2O9","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":26.0,"H":38.0,"N":2.0,"O":9.0},"names":{"en":"Remogliflozin etabonate"},"descriptions":{"en":"Remogliflozin etabonate (INN/USAN) is a drug of the gliflozin class for the treatment of non-alcoholic steatohepatitis (\"NASH\") and type 2 diabetes. Remogliflozin was discovered by the Japanese company Kissei Pharmaceutical and is currently being developed by BHV Pharma, a wholly owned subsidiary of North Carolina, US-based Avolynt, and Glenmark Pharmaceuticals through a collaboration with BHV. In 2002, GlaxoSmithKline (GSK) received a license to use it. From 2002 to 2009, GSK carried out a significant clinical development program for the treatment of type-2 diabetes mellitus in various nations across the world and obesity in the UK."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":9871420,"mass":522.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCOC(=O)OC[C@@H]1[C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H](O1)OC2=NN(C(=C2CC3=CC=C(C=C3)OC(C)C)C)C(C)C)O)O)O","inchikey":"UAOCLDQAQNNEAX-ABMICEGHSA-N","iupac":"ethyl [(2R,3S,4S,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-[5-methyl-1-propan-2-yl-4-[(4-propan-2-yloxyphenyl)methyl]pyrazol-3-yl]oxyoxan-2-yl]methyl carbonate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"9871420","atoms":75,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.088,"y":1.748,"z":-0.254,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.908,"y":1.234,"z":1.87,"el":"O"},{"x":1.507,"y":5.29,"z":1.078,"el":"O"},{"x":1.136,"y":4.856,"z":-1.756,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.619,"y":3.948,"z":2.614,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.234,"y":1.019,"z":-2.9,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.995,"y":-1.064,"z":-2.835,"el":"O"},{"x":0.826,"y":-0.506,"z":-1.535,"el":"O"},{"x":4.308,"y":-2.398,"z":0.269,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.304,"y":-0.853,"z":0.291,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.663,"y":0.295,"z":0.568,"el":"N"},{"x":0.49,"y":